Q1: Why did you leave FPT Software?

"I had a solid three years at FPT, but I felt it was time to step out of my comfort zone. I wanted to explore new challenges—especially having the chance to work with AI alongside OutSystems—and honestly, I was also looking for better career growth with a more competitive compensation package."

Q2: How do you feel about your current working environment and colleagues?

Honestly, I find the environment really good and dynamic. What I like most is the people—my colleagues are very friendly and supportive. 

Q3: How do you handle a tight deadline when unexpected bugs happen? (Xử lý áp lực & sự cố)

First, I don't panic. I assess the bug and immediately flag it to my lead so everyone is aligned. If the deadline is too close, I propose a workaround or a temporary fix first to keep the system running, then schedule proper refactoring later.

Q4: How do you learn new tech like AI while still doing OutSystems daily? (Đánh giá khả năng tự học)

I learn by doing. Instead of just reading theory, I try to integrate small AI features directly into my low-code practice—like connecting an external LLM API to an OutSystems app. That way, I upgrade my skills without slowing down my daily delivery.

Q5: What are your goals for the next 2–3 years? (Định hướng tương lai)

In the next 2 to 3 years, I want to become a go-to engineer who effectively bridges Low-code and AI. I want to build systems that are not just fast to deliver, but also intelligent and scalable.
